# T.K. - 6-Chapter Core Arc (Pair 1 - Character #2)
# Voice: Upbeat, buff, modern-life-loving Tikbalang adventurer who relies on his Nokia GPS because he gets himself lost.
# Rules: 90-95% English with light Filipino sprinkles. Zero parentheses. Zero time-of-day words. Zero em-dashes.
# Substitute Category: bottle ONLY in Ch. 3 (decided via dialogue choice -> allow_sub_cat:bottle).

label Greeting
if {Transaction_HasReactiveOpener}:
	TK: {Transaction_ReactiveOpener}

if {Transaction_Chapter} == 0.0:
	# Chapter 1: "Pin on the Map" (0 tallies)
	TK: Whew! Left by the balete, past the yellow fence, boom! Found your counter right on schedule!
	TK: Call me T.K., boss. Just moved down from the Kalumpang ridge to try proper barangay life!
	TK: Tell you what, paved street signs and this chunky Nokia GPS are humanity's finest inventions!
	- Welcome to Karimlan, T.K.
		TK: Salamat, boss! Already saved your storefront as Home Pin Number One on my keypad!
	- Took the scenic turn getting here?
		TK: Haha, sharp eyes! Not lost, boss, just testing extra cardio loops!
	- Cold drinks coming right up.
		TK: Solid! Electric fridges beat lukewarm mountain spring water any visit of the week!
	TK: Modern life really spoils a traveler, boss. Sneakers, cold coolers, maps that talk back!
	TK: Hook me up with [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] so I can rehydrate before my next lap!
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 1.0:
	# Chapter 2: "Inside-Out Pants" (Tally Inflection #1: +1 trapdoor OR +1 kind laugh / 0 tech / -1 mock)
	TK: Uy, boss, don't mind the seams. Wearing my hike pants inside out for, uh, airflow!
	TK: My Nokia swore the shortcut past the basketball half-court was a straight line to your awning.
	TK: Next blink, my laces are knotted to a bench and I've circled the same mango tree four times!
	TK: Lean in, boss. Folklore says tikbalangs lead folks astray, right? I'm the one tikbalang who gets himself lost!
	TK: That's why I love this Nokia GPS so much. Only thing keeping me out of the next province!
	if {Flag_PiloPunsoRattled}:
		- You skipped Tabi-tabi po by Pilo's mound!
			[signal arg="tally:+1"]
			[signal arg="note:Tipped T.K. off that he rattled Lolo Pilo's mango mound without saying Tabi-tabi po."]
			TK: Wait, the mango tree behind the half-court has a duwende mound?!
			TK: Grabe, no wonder my sneakers tied themselves! That explains everything, boss!
	- Your secret's safe. Nice inside-out shirt.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Kept T.K.'s funny directional secret safe and laughed kindly with him about his inside-out jersey."]
		TK: Haha, salamat, boss! Old habit from the ridge, baliktad shirt whenever the road spins!
		TK: Good knowing I don't have to pretend I'm a scary forest guide at this counter.
	- Maybe recalibrate your phone compass.
		[signal arg="note:Suggested T.K. recalibrate his Nokia GPS compass after his detour by the half-court."]
		TK: Good call, boss! Gotta check the settings once I catch my breath!
	- A tikbalang getting lost? Pretty embarrassing.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		[signal arg="note:Teased T.K. harshly about being a tikbalang with zero sense of direction."]
		TK: Ouch, boss. Hear enough of that from my uncles up on the mountain.
		TK: Whatever. Just grab my trail fuel so I can hit the road.
	TK: Pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] when you're free, boss. Four extra laps burned serious calories!
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 2.0:
	# Chapter 3: "One Bar Battery" (Single sunshower nod + True Name Reveal + allow_sub_cat:bottle -> +1 on SubstituteItem)
	[signal arg="flag:tk_true_name_known=true"]
	TK: Hey, don't look at me because of that sunny drizzle outside, boss! Nobody's getting married, I swear!
	TK: Rough trek. My Nokia battery died past the Kalumpang trailhead, and I walked straight into rice paddies!
	TK: Worse, an old neighbor recognized me and yelled my full mountain name across the whole canal!
	TK: Tiburcio Kalumpang. There, said it! Imagine a guy my size answering to Tiburcio at the gym!
	TK: Makes me feel like I'm just playing dress-up in sneakers. Pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], boss, old habit.
	- [Swap smoke for a cold bottle.]
		[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:bottle"]
		TK: Huh, boss? Why are you eyeing the cooler? I asked for smokes, same as my uncles!
		[end_timeline]
	- Tiburcio's a strong classic name.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Reassured T.K. that his birth name Tiburcio Kalumpang is nothing to be ashamed of."]
		TK: Wait, you're not laughing? Most folks expect a grandpa in a rocking chair, not me!
		TK: Salamat, boss. Still sticking to T.K. on the court, though you can keep that secret.
		TK: Alright, hand over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] while my phone cools off.
	- Pack spare batteries and stay home.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		[signal arg="note:Told T.K. to just rely on spare batteries and stay off the tougher trails."]
		TK: Yeah, maybe you're right, boss. No point hiking if one dead battery turns me around.
		TK: Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], salamat.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 3.0:
	# Chapter 4: "Offline Navigation" (Tally Inflection #3: +2 trapdoor / +1 respect / -1 stay on screen)
	TK: Uy, boss. Been staring at my Nokia screen since the creek bend, thinking hard.
	TK: Truth is, a real adventurer shouldn't panic every time a keypad battery hits zero.
	TK: Plus I owe Lolo Pilo a proper apology for stomping past his mango mound glued to my map.
	TK: How does a seven-foot modern gym horse make peace with a sixty-eight plaza legend?
	if {Flag_PiloWagerSet} or {Flag_PiloSubSweet}:
		- Bring candy and play him at Sipa!
			[signal arg="flag:tk_rematch_accepted=true"]
			[signal arg="tally:+2"]
			[signal arg="note:Advised T.K. to bring sweet candy for Lolo Pilo's mound and accept his Sipa challenge."]
			TK: Sipa?! With hooves this size?! Haha, I might kick that washer into orbit, boss!
			TK: Sweet candy for the mound and a fair match. Solid game plan, I'm in!
	- Pocket the phone and say Tabi-tabi po.
		[signal arg="flag:tk_rematch_accepted=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		[signal arg="note:Told T.K. to pocket his Nokia and greet Lolo Pilo properly with Tabi-tabi po."]
		TK: Fair and simple, boss. Eyes off the screen, proper bow to the old champ's tree.
		TK: Who knows, maybe he'll even teach me a trick or two about reading trails!
	- Stick to paved roads with signal.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		[signal arg="note:Advised T.K. to stick to paved streets with strong phone signal instead of visiting Lolo Pilo."]
		TK: Yeah, safer sticking where the five bars stay steady, I guess.
		TK: Shame though. Feels like I'm still dodging half the barangay.
	TK: Pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] first, boss, gotta fuel up!
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 4.0:
	# Chapter 5: "Sipa and Landmarks" (0 tallies - Ten Twist & Pair 1 Payoff)
	if {Flag_TKRematchAccepted} or {Flag_PiloWagerSet}:
		TK: Uy, boss! Check the jersey, right-side out, and my Nokia's clipped tight on my belt!
		TK: Went to the mango mound, boomed Tabi-tabi po, and took Lolo Pilo's Sipa challenge!
		TK: First kick launched his washer onto the barangay hall roof, then he drilled my ankle flick!
		TK: Best part? Carried him up the Kalumpang ridge on my shoulder so he could teach me moss and wind markers!
		TK: Best of both worlds now, boss. Five bars on the road, Lolo Pilo's landmarks in the woods!
		- Jersey's right-side out! Big progress!
			TK: Haha, zero wrong turns getting here! Even the balete bend looks crystal clear now!
		- How's the barangay hall roof holding?
			TK: Not a scratch, boss! Climbed up and grabbed his washer before the tanods even noticed!
		- Lolo Pilo make a tough coach?
			TK: Grabe, boss, tougher than any trainer! Made me keep ten kicks straight before letting me sit!
	else:
		TK: Uy, boss! Picked up two extra spare batteries for my Nokia down at the market!
		TK: Still steering wide around the mango mound just in case, though I wave politely when passing.
		TK: Guess old tricks and new gadgets run on separate lanes, ha?
		- Spare batteries never hurt on hikes.
			TK: True that, boss! Prepared is prepared, even if I still double-check every corner.
		- Still time to say hello to Pilo.
			TK: Maybe on a slower lap, boss! Right now I'm just sticking to the map pins.
	TK: Hook me up with [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color], boss, worked up a real sweat!
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 5.0:
	# Chapter 6: "Base Camp Karimlan" (Accumulated Tally Resolution -> 3 Bespoke Outcomes)
	if {Flag_TKRematchAccepted} and {Transaction_Tally} >= 3:
		[signal arg="outcome:trail_warden"]
		[signal arg="flag:tk_trail_warden=true"]
		[signal arg="note:T.K. gifted his Woven Travel Bandana threaded with a shed golden mane spine and claimed Karimlan as home."]
		TK: Hold up, boss! Put this right beside your register before I forget!
		TK: My woven travel bandana. Look close at the hem, see that single golden spine stitched in?
		TK: Old stories say mortals have to wrestle a tikbalang to win a mane spine. Forget that, friends get one freely.
		TK: Just guided a lost tricycle rider past the balete without checking my phone once, then played doubles with Lolo Pilo!
		if {Flag_TKTrueNameKnown}:
			- Honored to keep it, Tiburcio.
				TK: Haha, alright, you earned the right to call me Tiburcio behind this counter, boss!
		- Best trail guide in Karimlan.
			TK: Still keep my Nokia for the timer, boss, though my hooves finally know home!
		- [Fold the bandana neatly beside the register.]
			TK: Solid spot for it! Looks right at home on your counter wood!
		TK: Real talk, boss. Word on the ridge says that Pale Queen from Biringan comes weighing ledgers soon.
		TK: When she steps up to your awning, Karimlan's trail warden is standing right out front with you!
		TK: Now pass me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for the road, Home Pin Number One!
	elif {Transaction_Tally} >= 1:
		[signal arg="outcome:modern_strider"]
		[signal arg="note:T.K. settled in as a friendly, energetic regular who always calls out Tabi-tabi po past the mound."]
		TK: Uy, boss! Feeling right at home pounding these paved Karimlan roads!
		TK: Always shout a loud Tabi-tabi po past Lolo Pilo's mango tree now, zero knotted shoelaces!
		TK: Appreciate you keeping this counter stocked and welcoming for a mountain guy trying modern life!
		- Always got cold drinks ready, T.K.
			TK: Salamat, boss! Best pit stop on the whole barangay map!
		- Keep those laces double-knotted, T.K.
			TK: Haha, only by my own hands from here on out, boss!
		TK: Let me grab [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before my next ridge lap!
	else:
		[signal arg="outcome:restless_wanderer"]
		[signal arg="note:T.K. stayed a polite passing traveler relying strictly on his Nokia map pins."]
		TK: Uy, boss. Quick pit stop before my Nokia battery dips below three bars.
		TK: Paved roads are handy for a restock, though I'll probably keep moving along the highway trails.
		- Safe travels on the road, T.K.
			TK: Salamat, boss. Keep the cooler running cold.
		- What can I grab for you?
			TK: Fast and easy, just how I like a pit stop.
		TK: Just [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for my pack, salamat.
	[end_timeline]

label Talk
TK: No rush, boss! Just stretching my calves while my phone grabs signal.
- Almost got it, T.K.
	[end_timeline]
- Sorry T.K., we're out of stock.
	TK: Aw, sayang! All good, boss, I'll jog back after Mario drops off crates!
	[signal arg="refuse_service"]
	[end_timeline]

label Partial
set {Variation} = range(1,4).pick_random()
if {Variation} == 1.0:
	TK: Solid start, boss! Still need the rest for my trail pack!
elif {Variation} == 2.0:
	TK: Stashed that one! Take your time grabbing what's left, boss!
else:
	TK: Nice! No hurry on the rest, my knees appreciate the breather!
[end_timeline]

label SubstituteItem
[signal arg="flag:tk_sub_hydrate=true"]
[signal arg="tally:+1"]
[signal arg="note:Swapped T.K.'s frazzled cigarette request for cold {Transaction_SubstituteItemName} to keep his athletic streak alive."]
TK: Whoa, wait a second, boss!
TK: Handing me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_SubstituteItemName}[/color] instead of smokes?
TK: Haha, fair play! Nearly wrecked six months of trail cardio over one dead Nokia battery!
TK: Grabe, you look out for your regulars better than my gym spotter!
TK: Keep the change, boss. Cold hydration wins every round!
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label Satisfy
if {Transaction_StoryGouged}:
	TK: My wallet feels like it just hiked uphill with a boulder, boss.
	TK: Go a little easier on your Home Pin regular next pass, ha?
else:
	TK: Solid! Exactly what my legs needed, boss!
	if {Global_TipActive}:
		TK: Fair rate, boss! Keep the extra coins for your cooler bill!
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label WrongItem
TK: Uh, wrong trail marker, boss! Not quite what I asked for!
[end_timeline]
